tlp-panel (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The main menu can now pin the interface language to English or Turkish
    instead of following the locale. The choice is stored per user and read at
    startup.
  * The battery graphic reports state rather than just level: green while
    charging with motes drifting in, a highlight that sweeps the way the charge
    is going, red from 10% down instead of only at empty, and a slow pulse
    below 5%.
  * The fill now meets the outline with no gap and keeps a straight right-hand
    edge at every level.
  * The CPU speed limit scale says gigahertz.
  * python3-gi-cairo is now a declared dependency. The drawing has always
    needed it; the package only worked because something else usually pulls it
    in.

 -- Mehmet Emrah Tuncel <eylulsibelemrah@gmail.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 03:00:00 +0300

tlp-panel (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New CPU speed limit control: a slider over the frequency steps the scaling
    driver actually offers, writing CPU_SCALING_MAX_FREQ_ON_AC and _ON_BAT.
  * The system mode now drives the frequency ceiling as well. Automatic caps the
    processor on battery and lifts the cap on AC, Battery saving caps it either
    way, Full performance lifts it either way. Moving the slider overrides the
    limit for the power source in use until the next mode change.
  * Adaptive backlight no longer prints an "unsupported" line; the sliders stay
    greyed out instead. It shares a card with the CPU speed limit, and the card
    hides only when both are unavailable.

 -- Mehmet Emrah Tuncel <eylulsibelemrah@gmail.com>  Sat, 16 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0300

tlp-panel (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship an AppStream metainfo file. Without one the package installs but stays
    invisible in GNOME Software and KDE Discover; with it the app appears there
    by name, icon, screenshot and release notes.
  * Package the app for the AUR and publish a signed apt repository on GitHub
    Pages, so Debian and Ubuntu get updates through apt rather than a manual
    download each time.
  * Build the .deb in CI when a release is published, rather than by hand.
  * desktop-file-utils and appstream are now build dependencies; the build ran
    desktop-file-validate without declaring it.

 -- Mehmet Emrah Tunçel <timemrah@gmail.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 16:20:00 +0300

tlp-panel (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace AdwAboutDialog with a hand-built dialog. The stock widget renders
    its developer line as plain text, so the maintainer's address could
    neither sit beside the name nor be a link; setting it as comments filed it
    behind a Details page instead.
  * Capitalise the battery cycle count row to match its neighbours.

 -- Mehmet Emrah Tunçel <timemrah@gmail.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 03:45:00 +0300

